# Project Rules

- Before making changes, inspect the relevant existing code.
- Follow the current project architecture and naming conventions.
- Make only changes necessary for the requested task.
- Do not introduce new dependencies without approval.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Never read or expose production secrets.
- After implementation, run relevant available tests.
- Report changed files, verification results, and remaining risks.

## Change Approval

- Before modifying any project files, propose an implementation plan.
- Wait for explicit user approval before implementing the plan.
- Do not interpret a request for analysis or planning as approval to modify files.
- If approval has not been given, do not modify files.